# Suppressions for ADR-0024's vulnerability-scan CI job. Each entry needs a
# reason and a 30-day expiry (the waiver policy, see ADR-0024): an
# unreviewed, permanent ignore is how a real finding quietly stops being
# checked, and a short window costs little — worst case, someone spends two
# minutes confirming it's still unfixed and bumping the date. Expiring
# forces a revisit — either the fix has landed and the line becomes dead
# weight to delete, or it hasn't and the gate goes red again until someone
# looks.

# --- Frontend image: nothing to waive. Every Node-package CVE this image
# reported came from npm's own bundled dependency tree in the node:24-alpine
# base, not from package-lock.json; frontend/Dockerfile now deletes the
# package managers from the runtime stage, which the standalone server never
# invokes. The image scans clean with no suppressions at all — if a frontend
# entry is ever needed here again, check the reported PkgPath first, because
# a path under /usr/local/lib/node_modules means the removal regressed
# rather than that a new waiver is warranted.
